1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,047
Hi there!

2
00:00:01,047 --> 00:00:05,665
In this lesson, we're opening up Contacts,
the heart of your Kyntlo account.

3
00:00:05,665 --> 00:00:09,737
You'll learn to search, filter,
sort and arrange your contact list,

4
00:00:09,737 --> 00:00:13,079
and to save the views you
use every day as smart lists.

5
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:18,164
Every lead and customer who reaches
you, from a form, a phone call,

6
00:00:18,164 --> 00:00:20,753
a chat or an ad, lands here as a contact.

7
00:00:20,753 --> 00:00:24,479
Think of it as one shared
address book for your whole team,

8
00:00:24,479 --> 00:00:27,068
with each person's full history attached.

9
00:00:27,919 --> 00:00:32,433
Each row shows a person's phone number,
email, tags, where they came from,

10
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:34,324
and when they were last active.

11
00:00:34,324 --> 00:00:38,473
The number at the top tells you how
many contacts you have in total.

12
00:00:39,323 --> 00:00:42,484
The quickest way to find
someone is the search bar.

13
00:00:42,484 --> 00:00:45,954
Type part of a name, an email
address or a phone number,

14
00:00:45,954 --> 00:00:48,310
and the list narrows down as you type.

15
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:53,663
To narrow the list by what you know
about people, use Advanced Filters.

16
00:00:53,663 --> 00:00:57,533
Click Add filter, choose a field,
like Tag, and pick a value.

17
00:00:57,533 --> 00:01:00,387
Let's find everyone
interested in Invisalign.

18
00:01:01,237 --> 00:01:02,007
Click Apply.

19
00:01:02,007 --> 00:01:06,880
Now the list shows only matching contacts,
and the filter appears as a chip,

20
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:09,574
so you always know what you're looking at.

21
00:01:09,574 --> 00:01:12,075
Click the cross on a chip to remove it.

22
00:01:12,075 --> 00:01:13,999
You can stack several filters.

23
00:01:13,999 --> 00:01:16,949
A contact has to match
all of them to show up.

24
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:18,996
Next to it is Sort.

25
00:01:18,996 --> 00:01:22,019
By default, your newest
contacts are at the top.

26
00:01:22,019 --> 00:01:25,987
You can switch to oldest first,
or sort alphabetically by name.

27
00:01:25,987 --> 00:01:30,270
Alphabetical order is handy when
you're working through a call list.

28
00:01:31,121 --> 00:01:33,230
Want to see different information?

29
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:34,098
Click Columns.

30
00:01:34,098 --> 00:01:39,123
Tick the fields you care about, like the
team member each contact is assigned to,

31
00:01:39,123 --> 00:01:41,914
or a custom field such
as treatment interest.

32
00:01:41,914 --> 00:01:44,085
And untick the ones you don't need.

33
00:01:44,936 --> 00:01:49,101
Click Apply, and the list now shows
exactly what your team needs at a glance.

34
00:01:49,951 --> 00:01:51,242
Here's the best part.

35
00:01:51,242 --> 00:01:55,732
Once your filters, sort and columns
look right, click Save as smart list,

36
00:01:55,732 --> 00:01:56,900
and give it a name.

37
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,053
We'll call it Invisalign call list.

38
00:01:59,903 --> 00:02:03,455
Your new smart list appears
as a tab next to the others.

39
00:02:03,455 --> 00:02:04,913
It isn't a frozen copy.

40
00:02:04,913 --> 00:02:10,114
It updates itself, so new Invisalign leads
appear in it the moment they're tagged.

41
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,887
Click All to go back to everyone.

42
00:02:12,887 --> 00:02:15,627
You can also share a
smart list with teammates,

43
00:02:15,627 --> 00:02:17,842
so everybody works from the same view.

44
00:02:18,692 --> 00:02:19,760
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:23,529
Create one smart list for every
job your team does each day.

46
00:02:23,529 --> 00:02:28,177
For example, new leads from this week,
or patients who are due a check-up.

47
00:02:28,177 --> 00:02:32,825
Then your morning routine is simple:
open the list, work through it, done.

48
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:35,211
That's your contact list!

49
00:02:35,211 --> 00:02:39,879
In the next lesson, you'll add contacts
by hand, import a whole spreadsheet,

50
00:02:39,879 --> 00:02:42,458
and learn how Kyntlo keeps duplicates out.

51
00:02:42,458 --> 00:02:43,318
See you there.
